  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">Slashing is when the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-staking\"><strong id=\"\">stake</strong></a> delegated to a <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-node\"><strong id=\"\">validator node</strong></a> gets reduced - typically by burning (destroying) the staked tokens - as agreed under <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-consensus-protocol\"><strong id=\"\">consensus</strong></a> majority by the rest of the network.</p><p id=\"\">This is a <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-do-security-safety-and-liveness-mean\"><strong id=\"\">security</strong></a> feature that can be implemented within <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-proof-of-stake-pos-and-delegated-proof-of-stake-dpos\"><strong id=\"\">delegated proof of stake systems</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>to encourage validators to behave honestly or reliably, e.g. not sign a double spend <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-transaction-in-crypto\"><strong id=\"\">transaction</strong></a>.</p><p id=\"\">Slashing is highly complicated.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-proof-of-stake-pos-and-delegated-proof-of-stake-dpos\"><strong id=\"\">What's the difference between Proof of Stake (PoS) and Delegated Proof of Stake (DPoS)?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-sybil-attack\"><strong id=\"\">What is a Sybil attack?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-consensus-protocol\"><strong id=\"\">What is a consensus protocol?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-staking\"><strong id=\"\">What is staking?</strong></a></li></ul><p id=\"\">‍</p>",
